{"author":{"id":"038d65070aa747b6bc9d50939fa697ec871a40ed259db54429b255bbef2581d6"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792795225,"nonce":"Y3cIy4EAN1hOMJDiO1DjXmi4vb8=","title":"Add optional account preferences sync with local conflict handling","message":"Master roadmap: 455de32231e2b4a39765b4dff0223570b525ccec145049431e6483f5aa521f98\n\nMilestone: P5\n\nScope\nOffer opt-in sync of explicitly selected portable preferences such as theme/key bindings and extension selections, with versioning/conflict review and device context. Exclude credentials, workspace source, absolute local recent-project paths, machine-specific runners and caches unless separately designed and authorized. Keep per-workspace and per-team overrides distinct from personal account preferences.\n\nAcceptance criteria\nTwo devices converge or surface a clear conflict while offline/local settings remain editable. A new sign-in does not overwrite settings silently or leak paths/tokens. Turning sync off, deleting account data and switching personal/team contexts have deterministic behavior without periodic wakeups in a signed-out editor.\n\nAssociations and blocking dependencies are recorded below using full git-bug IDs. This issue remains open until implementation and validation are complete.","files":null}]}